
integer operators must have operands of matching size and type

integer literals default to i32

integer literals will be automatically transformed to match the
size and type of the other argument, if it can be done losslessly

enum values are treated as equivalent to their underlying integer
type for this purpose

enum values have an associated integer type with the default being
u32 if unspecified

smaller-than-wordsize integer types are zero or sign extended when
loaded from memory

larger integer types must be truncated with an explicit cast to be
stored in a smaller sized container


struct layout is done in the order fields are defined

1, 2, and 4 byte fields are aligned to an offset that is a multiple
of their size

larger fields are aligned on 4 byte offets (target dependent)


